949 0 obj
<<
/A 3628 0 R
/Alt (The flowchart details a systematic literature review process, structured vertically into three main stages: Identification, Screening, and Included. The Identification stage begins with a box labeled Studies from databases slash registers \(n equals 3900\), listing Scopus \(n equals 2026\) and Web of Science \(n equals 1874\). An arrow points from this box to a box labeled References removed \(n equals 834\), which specifies Duplicates identified manually \(n equals 6\) and Duplicates identified by Covidence \(n equals 828\). A downward arrow connects the initial studies box to the Screening stage, entering a box labeled Studies screened \(n equals 3066\). From this box, an arrow points right to Studies excluded \(n equals 2698\). Another downward arrow leads to Studies sought for retrieval \(n equals 367\). An arrow from this box points right to Studies not retrieved \(n equals 0\). A further downward arrow leads to Studies assessed for eligibility \(n equals 367\). From this box, an arrow points right to Studies excluded \(n equals 303\), which lists reasons: Simulation \(n equals 8\), Non English \(n equals 1\), No intervention \(n equals 182\), Not peer-reviewed \(n equals 20\), Wrong intervention \(n equals 34\), No full-text available \(n equals 12\), Review \(not-original-study\) \(n equals 17\), and Wrong target group \(no house-holds\) \(n equals 29\). Last box indicates the number of Studies included in review \(n equals 64\).)
/K 2
/P 45 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
